  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Record a deterministic inventory and immutable identification method for the selected source files, with origin, synthetic classification, usage/license evidence status, and material limitations, without modifying dataset/.",
    "Recommend one bounded scenario family, line of business, and policy-jurisdiction scope grounded in the available evidence, clearly identifying any remaining sponsor or qualified-domain-expert approval.",
    "Specify additional synthetic cases or perturbation classes, their provenance, labels, independent review needs, and separation from untouched source records.",
    "Define controlled comparison rules for research variants A-E, including common inputs and evidence, frozen configuration, repeated runs where applicable, scoring, and treatment of failed, abstained, or escalated output.",
    "Define benchmark versioning and freeze rules, partitions, leakage prevention, random seeds or deterministic alternatives, run manifests, and change invalidation rules.",
    "Define applicable metric calculations, evidence, aggregation, uncertainty reporting, evaluator authority, and a baseline-driven threshold approval method without using model judges as the sole basis for safety claims.",
    "Record validity limits and preserve the synthetic/public-only Vertex AI boundary, human authority, and prohibition on production, clinical, fraud, coverage, or payment-validity claims.",
    "Provide concrete downstream inputs and explicitly deferred decisions for DATA-001, POLICY-001, PLATFORM-001, and later experiment tasks without selecting unapproved contracts, schemas, frameworks, providers, or hosting."
  ],
